  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "locked",
      "x": 2320,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "LOCKED: the leftmost, Beaded pushed further.\\n\\nNow in the codebase as STAMP in lib/brand.ts and the Stamp component. The ring geometry went in with it \u2014 ringTypeBaseline and GLYPH_CENTER, plus a note recording the letter-spacing correction that is measurably wrong and should not be re-added.\\n\\nThe other three stay for reference."
    },
    {
      "id": "emblem",
      "x": 2320,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "VIBE over CORP, from the unbeaded construction.\\n\\nShort words change the problem. CERTIFIED filled about three quarters of its arc; VIBE fills a third at the same size, so the shoulders open and the ring goes slack. The fix is bigger, wider-tracked type \u2014 or more stars.\\n\\nThe two applications disagree: the hat wants shape, the badge wants words. Option B is the compromise.\n\nBottom row: the rainbow treatment. It is a TREATMENT \u2014 it needs full-colour printing, so the flat emblem stays canonical for stamps, embroidery and anything single-colour."
    }
  ],
